{
  "result": "I'd make it impossible to dehumanize another person.\n\nNot make everyone agree. Not make everyone kind, or selfless, or the same. Just remove that one mental trick where another person stops feeling quite as real as you do.\n\nYou could still be angry at them. Still compete with them, argue with them, think they're completely wrong. But underneath it you'd know \u2014 not intellectually, viscerally \u2014 that they're experiencing their life from the inside with the same intensity you're experiencing yours. Their fear feels like your fear. Their humiliation, their hope, their love for their kid.\n\nSo much cruelty depends on being able to switch that off. So does so much indifference.\n\nThe world would still have pain and scarcity and stupid, hard trade-offs. It wouldn't be utopia. But we'd have to face those things honestly, without first convincing ourselves that the people on the other side don't count in quite the same way.\n\nI think almost everything else would slowly have to change after that.",
